{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/285118-experience-weapons-and-other-gmc-conversions","id":285118,"title":"Experience, weapons, and other GMC conversions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-17T10:40:19-07:00","id":285118,"title":"Experience, weapons, and other GMC conversions","content":"Has anyone come up with an appropriate conversion of experience for Geist? Seems like the old system handled experience on a much larger scale.<br /> <br /> As a note: I would like to have rules that allow a long term game - I'm a little concerned that GMC makes experience come on much faster than it was originally intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T11:53:34-07:00","id":285184,"title":"","content":"Just hand out less? Personally, I've stuck with the old experience system as far as Geist is concerned. If you're concerned about your PC's raising too quickly to too high levels of capabillity in a single field given the linear ex-cost of things in the new system, just kindly tell your players not to min-max their characters. Thats something I allready did, back in the old system.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could allways try to implement some kind of experience-sink for your players. I play this one scenario, in which one of the other PC's has gotten some strange hedronic artifact that lets him do pretty much anything he desires, but siphons a bit of experience points each time he uses it. It could be easy to throw some underworld artifact in, which decays the players memories each time it is used.<br /> <br /> Any of that sounds reasonable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T12:48:40-07:00","id":285212,"title":"","content":"I think if anything I'll stick to the old experience costs - although I do like the new beat system. Using the beat system, I suspect players will be able to get 5 beats a session if they're really good (more realistically 1 every two sessions)<br /> <br /> I may hand out full experience points on occasion for story completion - or at least 3-4 beats at a time) to help balance it out - but I get the feeling that players will power up too quickly to maintain long lasting campaigns if I don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T15:20:07-07:00","id":285460,"title":"","content":"I'd make Keys like 2 Experiences, Manifestations like 5 or 6.<br /> <br /> ~5 beats a session give or take is the intent, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T07:42:40-07:00","id":285911,"title":"","content":"oh, I should clarify, 1 exp every two sessions, not one beat.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking I just want the costs of more powerful manifestations to ramp up. Upgrading from the 2 to 3 dot version of curse should be more expensive then getting it initially. Keys will probably remain relatively cheap in comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T09:18:48-07:00","id":286679,"title":"","content":"Before I go into details: I should point out that I'm leaning towards trying the GM as written and seeing how things go after the first 3 sessions or so. That said, here's how I'm thinking of converting:<br /> <br /> Experience houserules:<br /> <br /> Costs are using the god machine rules with the following addendum: The first 1-2 dots in anything is base cost, 3-4 is double and 5th dot in anything is tripled. Stats where this is not appropriate are subject to GM approval (as are 5th dot buys) Costs are:<br /> <br /> Attribute: 4 dots (Addendum applies)<br /> Synergy: 3 dots (Addendum does not apply but subject to GM approval)<br /> Merit: 1 Experience (Addendum applies)<br /> Skill: 2 Experiences (Addendum applies)<br /> Specialty: 1 Experience (Flat cost)<br /> Willpower: 1 Experience (Flat cost)<br /> <br /> Ceremony: 1 Experience per dot (Flat cost)<br /> Key: 2 Experiences (Flat cost)<br /> Manifestation: 3 dots (Addendum applies)<br /> Psyche: 4 experiences (Flat cost, subject to GM approval)<br /> <br /> Also, I'm considering if Rage powers and shroud need to be modified after the GM update. I've got Strix and Blood and smoke coming in the mail, so I'll have to see if they'll give me a good idea. Is there anything else that might need to be tweaked? Looks like armor and weapon values are the majority of the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}